445
00:37:53,841 --> 00:37:57,980
and it was what I view the old-time hardware store.

446
00:37:57,981 --> 00:38:03,800
It was the place where you would go in and there were cabinets and cubby holes of old wood drawers.

447
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:08,740
And, you know, you'd go in there and talk to Gus, who was one of the guys that worked there at the time,

448
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:14,320
and say, you know, I need a small screw to go inside this lamp and I'm not quite sure what size it is.

449
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:16,560
And this guy was in the hardware business forever.

450
00:38:16,620 --> 00:38:20,980
And he'd say, what you need is a quarter-twenty screw that's, you know, an inch and a quarter long.

451
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:25,120
And he'd walk over, he'd open up this drawer, pull it out, hand it to you and send you on your way.

452
00:38:25,121 --> 00:38:34,280
It was somebody that had that experience, and there was a look and a feel in that kind of hardware store that kind of is a dying phenomenon.

453
00:38:34,460 --> 00:38:38,120
You don't see that as much just because things are being modernized and remodeled.

454
00:38:39,060 --> 00:38:45,380
But those same people, in my mind, and I still experience it every day, still exist in that business.

455
00:38:46,380 --> 00:38:53,620
I know you drive around the suburbs today, and you see these big, huge orange boxes that sell hardware.

456
00:38:53,621 --> 00:38:56,160
and I love to go in those places.

457
00:38:56,560 --> 00:38:59,220
I think of those places as sort of Disneyland, you know,

458
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:00,600
because they've got so much.

459
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:02,580
But I like to go in the little places too

460
00:39:02,581 --> 00:39:05,800
and there's always going to be a place for the mom and pop

461
00:39:05,801 --> 00:39:09,640
because you can't put one of these big orange boxes on every corner.

462
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,760
You've got to have the neighborhood hardware store

463
00:39:12,761 --> 00:39:15,220
when you just need one screw.

464
00:39:15,600 --> 00:39:18,540
You know, you're not going to run eight miles

465
00:39:18,541 --> 00:39:21,540
to get that one screw and save two cents.

466
00:39:21,541 --> 00:39:28,520
still the number of big boxes continues to grow while the smaller stores dwindle in number

467
00:39:28,521 --> 00:39:34,615
in 1955 there were 35,000 hardware stores in the u.s.

468
00:39:34,616 --> 00:39:39,560
by 1994 the number had dropped to less than

469
00:39:39,561 --> 00:39:49,200
30,000 today there are around 14,000 i really don't think you can compare a hardware store

470
00:39:49,201 --> 00:39:50,280
with the big box stores.

471
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:52,960
They're really two separate types of operations.

472
00:39:53,440 --> 00:39:56,660
Hardware stores have really been the foundation of small-town America.

473
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:59,280
They started really serving their individual communities,

474
00:39:59,380 --> 00:40:02,480
being right inside the town, very close to all the traffic,

475
00:40:02,481 --> 00:40:06,160
where people could really come and get whatever they needed for their home,

476
00:40:06,500 --> 00:40:10,260
whether it was for cooking or it was for building or repairing.

477
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:12,180
It was all right here in the hardware store.

478
00:40:13,540 --> 00:40:16,860
And just when we thought the hardware store couldn't get any bigger,

479
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:19,840
The biggest hardware store of all has arrived.

480
00:40:20,660 --> 00:40:23,180
The tonnage of hardware available via the Internet

481
00:40:23,181 --> 00:40:27,540
makes the biggest big box look like a nail bin at a mom-and-pop store.

482
00:40:28,420 --> 00:40:32,480
Well, the Internet has changed the hardware business and the hardware store business somewhat,

483
00:40:32,600 --> 00:40:35,800
and it promises to change it as the future comes to us.

484
00:40:37,220 --> 00:40:42,420
The Internet allows folks to research information about products, tools, services,

485
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:45,880
and availability of things before they come to the store in many cases.

486
00:40:45,881 --> 00:40:52,300
So frequently we're dealing with a much better educated shopper who has spent time on the Internet looking for information about the project

487
00:40:52,301 --> 00:40:54,540
and knows a little bit more about what they're looking for.

488
00:40:55,100 --> 00:40:59,740
It also changes the shopping experience somewhat as we integrate the Internet into the store.

489
00:41:00,060 --> 00:41:05,940
It allows us a greater selection of merchandise in the store that may not actually be stocked there but is available through the store.

490
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:12,640
If you look at TrueValue.com, this has thousands of pages of home improvement advice

491
00:41:12,641 --> 00:41:17,700
and active sections where you can actually ask questions to experts.

492
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,560
This certainly is a community in and of itself.

493
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:29,720
But some old-school hardwareian types will always need the tactile reality of cold steel and raw tape.

494
00:41:29,880 --> 00:41:33,920
For me, hardware is definitely a touchy-feely situation.

495
00:41:34,180 --> 00:41:38,020
It's something that even if it's a project that is not my own,

496
00:41:38,021 --> 00:41:45,360
I need to know that it's going to be faithful to the application to which I am using it for.

497
00:41:46,180 --> 00:41:47,920
I have to see it and touch it.

498
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:51,320
I don't think that a picture on a computer screen is going to do that for me.

499
00:41:52,060 --> 00:41:56,200
I think having hardware online is really a necessity of where we are in America today

500
00:41:56,201 --> 00:41:59,060
where people don't have the time to do all the things that we'd like to do.

501
00:41:59,500 --> 00:42:03,320
But I think what True Value has been able to do is sort of replicate some of that special spirit

502
00:42:03,321 --> 00:42:06,920
of the American hardware store by creating a site that allows you to get that information

503
00:42:06,921 --> 00:42:08,580
and that product in the same visit.

504
00:42:09,680 --> 00:42:12,560
I don't understand buying hardware online.

505
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:14,820
For one thing, when I buy hardware,

506
00:42:15,040 --> 00:42:17,300
I usually buy hardware in a rush, in a pinch,

507
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:18,660
because I need it right now.

508
00:42:18,980 --> 00:42:20,840
It's not something I plan ahead on.

509
00:42:20,980 --> 00:42:22,620
I can't see that this is going to happen,

510
00:42:22,740 --> 00:42:26,000
that online hardware stores will take over for

511
00:42:26,001 --> 00:42:28,160
the actual hardware store experience.

512
00:42:30,460 --> 00:42:32,720
The hardware store experience.

513
00:42:33,140 --> 00:42:34,520
Is that what this is all about?

514
00:42:34,521 --> 00:42:39,100
Americans spend countless hours and billions of dollars each year on hardware.

515
00:42:39,760 --> 00:42:42,700
What does our love for this ritual say about our society?

516
00:42:43,620 --> 00:42:49,080
The hardware store contradicts that idea that we throw everything away in our society.

517
00:42:49,240 --> 00:42:50,960
At least in this area, we don't.

518
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:57,400
And the hardware store is a kind of, it's almost like a shrine to the history of house building.

519
00:42:57,401 --> 00:43:02,980
And you can find all these old bits and pieces that you need to keep your house going.

520
00:43:02,981 --> 00:43:10,880
I live in an old house, for instance, and if I need to replace something, I go to a good local hardware store, they carry it.

521
00:43:10,940 --> 00:43:17,340
There's some little manufacturer in Ohio who still turns out this little piece of hardware that you need to fix a lock with.

522
00:43:18,580 --> 00:43:25,240
What I think is very interesting about the hardware stores is it's the kind of place that people will visit two or three times a week.

523
00:43:25,620 --> 00:43:30,180
Many times two or three times a day if you're in the middle of a project, which drives you crazy.

524
00:43:30,181 --> 00:43:35,820
but it's always there for you, and there's always going to be a place for the hardware store.

525
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:40,720
I mean, yes, there are the big box stores that exist, and they do have a lot of things,

526
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:46,840
but that personal service that you get and the kind of attention to detail from your local hardware store,

527
00:43:47,180 --> 00:43:50,060
in my opinion, will never be equaled.

528
00:43:51,240 --> 00:43:57,420
So maybe for some, the appeal of the hardware store is a little like taking a ride in a technology time machine.

529
00:43:58,220 --> 00:44:01,380
They can visit the past while they take a glimpse into the future.

530
00:44:03,200 --> 00:44:08,220
For the rest of us, well, we just need to fix a leaky faucet.

531
00:44:09,240 --> 00:44:11,740
Nor that darn hinge on the bathroom door.

